    "body": "This feature issue is based on a discussion in issue #2304 \r\n>> Another problem in context of this topic is that (to my understanding) only people with \"editing\" permissions are allowed to investigate the audit trail.\r\n\r\n>Indeed it is true. I wasn't really aware of this and will make the necessary changes so it can be accessed in view mode, too.\r\n\r\nAs it turns out, the access to the audit trail is very broad and more fine control is needed. According to GDPR regulations, it must be possible to delete GDPR related data from electronic systems like elabFTW. In contrast to be compliant with FDA's \"21 CFR part 11\"  an audit trail recording all changes is needed. Both statements are somewhat exclusive to my opinion. The only solution I see is that access to an audit trail can be narrowed down to very limited number of people, at least for some specific experiment. \r\n@NicolasCARPi  Do you have any more ideas?\r\n\r\nIdeally, access settings for audit trail can be also enforced by admins to ensure that the system configurations are compliant as stated above.\r\n",
